\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3}Quantifying the prescription dependence}{19}{section*.34}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces Fractional prescription dependence $\Delta A/A\equiv (A_{\rm  DP}-A_{\rm  TP})/A_{\rm  TP}$ of the calibrated foam amplitude, evaluated under the constraint that the differential-primary (DP) and total-primary (TP) anchorings reproduce the \emph  {same} observed phase variance $\sigma _\phi ^2$ for each source. TP weights the differential $d[(D_C/\ell _P)^{2-2\alpha }]$ of the calibrated total formula~\eqref  {eq:np-total} by $(1+z')^2$; DP weights a uniform per-comoving-shell element (normalized to the same total) by $(1+z')^2$; the two coincide identically at $\alpha =1/2$ and in the $z\to 0$ limit. Fiducial cosmology: flat Planck~2018 ($\Omega _m=0.315$, $H_0=67.36$\,km\,s$^{-1}$\,Mpc$^{-1}$)~\cite  {Aghanim2020}, with $D_C$ evaluated to $z=0.151$ (GRB\,221009A) and $z_{\rm  LS}=1089.8$ (CMB). The GRB row stays at the percent level, confirming the historical invisibility of the anchoring ambiguity; the CMB row reaches tens of percent at the holographic $\alpha =2/3$ and is fully degenerate ($-100\%$) at $\alpha =1$, where the total-primary differential vanishes --- the CMB amplitude is prescription-limited, not data-limited.}}{19}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:prescription}{{II}{19}{Fractional prescription dependence $\Delta A/A\equiv (A_{\rm DP}-A_{\rm TP})/A_{\rm TP}$ of the calibrated foam amplitude, evaluated under the constraint that the differential-primary (DP) and total-primary (TP) anchorings reproduce the \emph {same} observed phase variance $\sigma _\phi ^2$ for each source. TP weights the differential $d[(D_C/\ell _P)^{2-2\alpha }]$ of the calibrated total formula~\eqref {eq:np-total} by $(1+z')^2$; DP weights a uniform per-comoving-shell element (normalized to the same total) by $(1+z')^2$; the two coincide identically at $\alpha =1/2$ and in the $z\to 0$ limit. Fiducial cosmology: flat Planck~2018 ($\Omega _m=0.315$, $H_0=67.36$\,km\,s$^{-1}$\,Mpc$^{-1}$)~\cite {Aghanim2020}, with $D_C$ evaluated to $z=0.151$ (GRB\,221009A) and $z_{\rm LS}=1089.8$ (CMB). The GRB row stays at the percent level, confirming the historical invisibility of the anchoring ambiguity; the CMB row reaches tens of percent at the holographic $\alpha =2/3$ and is fully degenerate ($-100\%$) at $\alpha =1$, where the total-primary differential vanishes --- the CMB amplitude is prescription-limited, not data-limited}{table.2}{}}
